1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:10,688
Dentists, accountants and advocates are trusted with client details.
One chatbot paste can give them away.

2
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:16,236
Professionals paste client notes into chatbots.
The name goes with it.

3
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:30,425
Here the note is cleaned inside the browser first.
Names, phones, dates and IDs become labels.

4
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:36,984
This is everything the cloud will see.
No name, no phone, no relative.

5
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:55,768
The cloud writes the letter.
The browser puts the names back.

6
00:01:09,997 --> 00:01:14,997
This is the request, as sent.
Labels only, no identifiers.

7
00:01:35,997 --> 00:01:41,594
Offline, the on-device model still works.
The letter waits, then sends itself.

8
00:01:52,147 --> 00:01:58,192
Same engine, three professions.
For the accountant, amounts and sections stay visible.

9
00:02:03,647 --> 00:02:07,559
For the advocate, IDs and settlement sums are hidden.

10
00:02:23,290 --> 00:02:37,997
On 300 generated notes, about two to four percent of identifiers were left.
On 40 realistic notes written with an AI assistant, about three in ten.
Small sets. You check every note before it is sent.

11
00:02:40,190 --> 00:02:46,001
Firebase AI Logic, Gemini Nano, App Check.
Try it at the link below.
